## Quickstart

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Requirements: Jetson AGX Thor (JetPack 7.x, `sm_110a`), Docker + NVIDIA Container Toolkit, [`uv`](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/).

```bash
# the CLI (the package is mjolnir-cli; the command is `mjolnir`)
uv tool install mjolnir-cli

# one-time: Thor host setup for stable numbers (clocks, power mode, fans, swap)
mjolnir hw setup

# serve: Qwen3.8-27B NVFP4 on the Mjolnir image, --attention-backend MJOLNIR, port 6001
mjolnir serve up
```

```bash
curl -s http://localhost:6001/v1/chat/completions \
  -H 'content-type: application/json' \
  -d '{"model": "{{ ctx.model }}", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "hi"}], "max_tokens": 64}'
```

**Use the image directly** (any model, any vLLM flags):

```bash
docker run --rm -it --gpus all --ipc host -p 8000:8000 -e VLLM_KV_CACHE_LAYOUT=HND \
  {{ ctx.image }} <model> --kv-cache-dtype fp8 --attention-backend MJOLNIR
```

**Or bring your own vLLM {{ ctx.vllm_version }}**: `pip install mjolnir-kernel` registers the backend as `CUSTOM` through vLLM's plugin system (`--attention-backend CUSTOM`); [`thor-mjolnir-attention-backend.patch`](docker/vllm-thor/patches/thor-mjolnir-attention-backend.patch) adds the `MJOLNIR` name.

## Benchmarks

All kernel numbers are **ncu kernel time** (decode + split-KV merge), cold L2, base clocks, one sequence with 24 query / 4 KV heads, head dim 256, 128-token pages — the attention shape of Qwen3.8-27B — at **every context length from 128 to 256K tokens**. Legs:

| leg | what runs | KV cache |
|---|---|---|
| **Mjolnir · e2m3 KV** | this kernel, the default (6-bit KV read directly by the tensor cores; served by `{{ ctx.default_config }}`) | e2m3, head-major pages |
| **Mjolnir · fp8 KV** | this kernel on fp8 KV (`NVFP4_MJOLNIR`) | fp8 e4m3, head-major pages |
| **FlashInfer** | tensor-core decode as vLLM's FlashInfer backend runs it | fp8 e4m3, NHD pages |
| **FlashAttention 2** | `vllm_flash_attn` FA2 — stock vLLM {{ ctx.vllm_version }}'s `sm_110` default | bf16 <sup>(FA2 has no fp8 KV)</sup> |

Measured on a dedicated Thor: a same-run ratio repeats within ±{{ ctx.noise_pct }}% between runs, so ratios inside that band are drawn gray (L=16K is the exception — it is bimodal across runs; see [`docs/methodology/benchmarking.md`](docs/methodology/benchmarking.md)).

